Section 1- The Artifact Neuron consists of 4 ctfs

1. Neuron Meet 0: here we ran the cmd nc aureolin-pixie.cylabacademy.net 53452 on our powershell 
                  and were asked to write numbers between -10 and 10 and based on the number we 
                  entered the terminal would return either 1 (yes) or 0 (no) our goal is to make 
                  the terminal return the 1 or 0 in the pattern of “01110000” so we can get the 
                  flag from the terminal it specifies if the number entered should be only 
                  entered once and cannot be entered again immediately say we enter -1 twice and
                  it will be counted keeping in mind it was not entered right after you entered it
                  in the previous commit.

2. Neuron Meet 2D-0: it follows the same rules as the last challenge but here we have to enter 2 
                     numbers together from the range (-10,10) until we get the output pattern as
                     "01110000" it also follows the same rule that the same input used once cannot
                     be used as the very next input. 

3. Neuron Express 0: this challenge taught us about the perceptron rule i.e. w*x+b>=0 so i ran inputs like
                     0 and 1 and the output was stays quite but when i went with 2 3 5 it fired so i considered
                     w=1 and b= -2 that gave me x-2>=0 now on assigning values to x like 0 and 1 the output was
                     stays quite as we got the result < 0 on but same x = 3 will fire the output.

4. Neuron Express 2D-0: this is the same as the previous one but on a 2D plane here w1*x+w2*y+b>=0 so on trying x=2
                        that didnt make the output fire but as i did x=3 the output started firing and y well it didnt 
                        contribute much to change the classification. so the simplest equation was w1=1 w2=0 and b= -3
                        giving equation as 1x+0-3>=0 ---> x>=3 the rule says >= 0, so (3, anything) fires exactly at 
                        the boundary.

